<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9650" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντεπ-άγω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰγ</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead against</i>: abs. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατόν</span> or the like ), <i>advance
				against, advance to meet an enemy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.124
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.18.11
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inflict in return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποινήν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristaenet.
					2.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>introduce as a counter-measure,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλεξήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Onos.
					30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
